{title: When the Roll Is Called Up Yonder}
{artist: James Black}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 108}

Verse 1
When the [D]trumpet of the Lord shall sound and [G]time shall be no [D]more,
and the morning breaks eternal, bright, and [A]fair —
when the [D]saved of earth shall gather over [G]on the other [D]shore,
and the [A]roll is called up [D]yonder, I'll be there.

Chorus
[D]When the roll is called up [G]yon[D]der,
when the roll is called up [A]yonder,
[D]when the roll is called up [G]yon[D]der —
when the [A]roll is called up [D]yonder, I'll be there.

Verse 2
On that bright [D]and cloudless morning when the dead in Christ shall rise, And the [G]glory of His resurrection share; When [D]His chosen
ones shall gather to their home beyond the skies, And the roll [A]is called up
yonder, I'll be [D]there. When the roll is called up yonder, When the [G]roll is called up [D]yonder, When
the roll is [A]called up yonder, When the roll is [D]called up yonder, I'll be there.

Verse 3
Let us labor [D]for the Master from the dawn till setting sun, Let us talk [G]of all His wondrous love and care; [D]Then when
all of life is over, and our work on earth is done, [A]And the roll
is called up yonder, [D]I'll be there. When the roll is called up yonder, [G]When the roll is called [D]up yonder,
When the roll [A]is called up yonder, When the roll [D]is called up yonder, I'll be there.
